#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078230 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec980fcb-97ed-5c60-94de-0521d9d7df27" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Definite Integral of a Piecewise Continuous Function Given the Function Expression"}] :question/id #uuid "df884ed9-c75e-5a38-abe2-425e01ee4aa7" :question/math-academy-id "e-432" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined below. What is the value of $\\displaystyle \\int_{-2}^5 f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x\\,?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3, & x<0 \\\\ 2x+3, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}3\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{5}(2x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3x{|}_{-2}^{0}+({x}^{2}+3x){|}_{0}^{5} \\\\  & =[3(0)-3(-2)]+[({5}^{2}+3(5))-({0}^{2}+3(0))] \\\\  & =6+25+15 \\\\  & =46.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078231 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4abe11e-febf-5461-96ee-bca8a7713bdf" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Definite Integral of a Piecewise Linear Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/id #uuid "317454f0-3a04-5c1c-a451-2b8b2ec850ac" :question/math-academy-id "e-433" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036389/assets/ad45cbdcd126df931f1a35c60ca12b45d520a2a0a5cddf4fa012c0515d3024c7.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of two line segments. Find the value of $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{4} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of two parts: the line segment for $x \\in [0,2)$ and the line segment for $x \\in [2,4].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{4} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x = \\underbrace{\\int_{0}^{2} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x}_{A_1} + \\underbrace{\\int_{2}^{4} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x}_{-A_2}.\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x \\in [0,2).$ The corresponding region is a rectangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =bh \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x \\in [2,4].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n\\int_{2}^{4} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x =-A_2 = -2.\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2} \\\\  & =4-2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078232 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb30dbbf-4f83-59d0-b712-f0e592aafb27" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Definite Integral of a Piecewise Curved Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/id #uuid "189d4a9a-fb2c-57b2-b9f6-9bec14fa1062" :question/math-academy-id "e-434" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036389/assets/36c6a1c84e0b0c32a5fd35fd422645f60340da6d205dd8cc31054cd558c2f5f9.png)\n\nGiven the graph of $y=f(x)$ above, find the value of $\\displaystyle \\int_{-4}^4 f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of four parts: the arc of a semi-circle for $x\\in [-4,0],$ a line segment for $x\\in (0,2),$ a line segment for $x\\in (2,4],$ and the point at $x=2.$ So, we can use the additive property of integrals to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-4}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={{{\\int }_{-4}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}+0+{{{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x \\in [-4,0].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle with a radius of $2,$ so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x \\in (0,2).$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{2} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x = -A_2 = -2.\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x \\in (2,4].$  The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2}+{A}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\pi -2+2 \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296668 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4abe11e-febf-5461-96ee-bca8a7713bdf" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Definite Integral of a Piecewise Linear Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03f1af6f-a432-58bb-a999-4cd67fd6fa93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296670} {:answer/id #uuid "f95ca29d-d08a-5b85-9f41-f3a7fb4bdd4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296671} {:answer/id #uuid "cc84a1b4-4b51-505e-a8bc-365bdc846107" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296672} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f6f531-5914-5ed2-bc2f-e3069da9a038" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296673} {:answer/id #uuid "cccf8bd7-143b-5651-84fb-374769cf2501" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2f6f531-5914-5ed2-bc2f-e3069da9a038" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296673} :answer-field/id #uuid "97582334-4c92-5acc-b560-b65db03a5215" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296669}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a3e6f460-32b8-5013-a35b-ba52c5b54bbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-18004" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036389/assets/d43fa0efcfb8788316c86958b1175741c136588e81a8119131d1ca0f8d8ee229.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of four line segments. Find the value of ${\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of four parts: the line segment for $x\\in [-3,-2),$ the line segment for $x\\in [-2,-1),$ the line segment for $x\\in [-1,1),$ and the line segments for $x\\in [1,3].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-3}^{-2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}+{{{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{4}}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-3,-2).$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-2,-1).$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-1.\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-1,1).$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $4$th integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [1,3].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{4}=-2.\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2}+{A}_{3}-{A}_{4} \\\\  & =1-1+2-2 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289657 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec980fcb-97ed-5c60-94de-0521d9d7df27" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Definite Integral of a Piecewise Continuous Function Given the Function Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cf407f2-5989-55ec-8135-061fe831e33d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cf407f2-5989-55ec-8135-061fe831e33d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289659} :answer-field/id #uuid "97084882-fc93-5592-8a8d-200228f92323" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289658}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a4321dc5-5a1f-5eae-acf4-e27f4a92f7a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-341981" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x-5, & x<2, \\\\ 1, & x\\ge 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-4}^{2}(\\frac{1}{2}x-5)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{2}^{6}1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}-5x){|}_{-4}^{2}\\,+\\,x{|}_{2}^{6} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{4}(2)^{2}-5(2)\\,-\\,(\\frac{1}{4}(-4)^{2}-5(-4))]\\,+\\,[\\,6-2\\,] \\\\  & =[1-10\\,-\\,(4+20)]+4 \\\\  & =[-9-24]+4 \\\\  & =-33+4 \\\\  & =-29.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296695 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb30dbbf-4f83-59d0-b712-f0e592aafb27" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Definite Integral of a Piecewise Curved Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd8038c8-1046-58e8-84f0-5162159f0c32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi +16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296697} {:answer/id #uuid "48776417-a438-5f07-b0e6-d31ef8f8314d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi +8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296698} {:answer/id #uuid "891c1d62-d5a1-5127-b5aa-b14807a51b4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi +4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296699} {:answer/id #uuid "b7fb9a25-3870-5d8e-9e54-d2c4d0f5d3fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi +4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296700} {:answer/id #uuid "102e1f8a-f770-53ca-91bf-9d06ba760e7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi +8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48776417-a438-5f07-b0e6-d31ef8f8314d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi +8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296698} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a261122-1a15-5bfa-8e2c-cf52c60b75a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "97f5c0c0-1b45-5f58-be76-fdc17942bba8" :question/math-academy-id "q-353387" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036389/assets/877771be920838a330edabe84b07eb817f1f3d7f1343b6866b9c2f078e079a67.png)\n\nGiven the graph of $y=f(x)$ above, find the value of \n${\\int }_{-4}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of $2$ parts: the arc of the semi-circle for $x\\in [-4,0)$ and the line segment for $x\\in [0,4].$ So, we can use the additive property of integrals to get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-4}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-4,0).$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot (2)^{2} \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,4].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}b\\cdot h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =2\\pi +8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078946 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb30dbbf-4f83-59d0-b712-f0e592aafb27" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Definite Integral of a Piecewise Curved Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7304737-cba6-5fbc-b8be-0f1ac860d786" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10 + \\frac{π}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076888} {:answer/id #uuid "27e19e5e-9ae9-55e3-a6b1-2d3041c09690" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 + π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076889} {:answer/id #uuid "2aa18fed-eec9-5887-a749-9f71fb14a6c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10 + π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076890} {:answer/id #uuid "2f8ad594-e424-5b7f-9948-5e8da6618757" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 + \\frac{π}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076891} {:answer/id #uuid "33d74abb-4ac1-5932-857d-5df1fe3e33ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10 + \\frac{3π}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7304737-cba6-5fbc-b8be-0f1ac860d786" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10 + \\frac{π}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076888} :answer-field/id #uuid "6463ff6a-e667-5122-8f6a-66c6d265d077" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076887}] :question/id #uuid "b82eafa4-95ed-5313-a838-9f9ba69b6d8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-49176" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/626/Source/Images/q-49176.png)\n\nGiven the graph of $y = f(x)$ above, find the value of\n$∫_{-2}^{5}f(x)dx$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078972 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec980fcb-97ed-5c60-94de-0521d9d7df27" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Definite Integral of a Piecewise Continuous Function Given the Function Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bcb1520b-235b-5cea-bacf-623ce39e2497" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077044} {:answer/id #uuid "d8b6c71d-8121-5aee-b9b2-bd10a0f6c04c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077045} {:answer/id #uuid "12060711-88b3-5b49-854b-07986d37ab6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077046} {:answer/id #uuid "4be47cff-d863-5011-b6f2-6fdb9673542c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077047} {:answer/id #uuid "7af1221c-ba06-5272-96e1-e9e202d9256d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7af1221c-ba06-5272-96e1-e9e202d9256d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077048} :answer-field/id #uuid "805565f6-24e6-51c1-97fb-51e6e8617a19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186077043}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f7ff75a6-3ae3-540e-8971-b7a98178dcaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-5046" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined below. What is the value of \n${\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}4, & x<0 \\\\ -x+4, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}4\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{4}(-x+4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4x{|}_{-3}^{0}+(-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+4x){|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =[4(0)-4(-3)]+[-\\frac{(4)^{2}}{2}+4(4)+\\frac{(0)^{2}}{2}-4(0)] \\\\  & =[0+12]+[-8+16+0-0] \\\\  & =12+8 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
